group: D6h
formula: C6H6
construction: its two sets of equivalent atoms
headline: 
note: Fragments: its two sets of equivalent atoms · energies in Hartree · labels in D<sub>6h</sub> · 6 core orbitals hidden
about: **What is drawn.** Drawn as its two sets of equivalent atoms. This molecule has no central atom, so there is no central-atom diagram; combining fragments of it instead needs a subgroup and a choice. The molecular levels in the middle are the calculation's own orbital energies, in Hartree.\n\n**Fragment levels.** Each fragment level is placed at the mean of the molecular orbitals it became, weighted by its share of them, and kept in the atom's own shell order. Its free-atom energy is given beside it.\n\n**Symmetry.** Symmetry labels computed from the orbitals in D6h; the code reported none.\n\n**The circles beside each symmetry orbital** show the atoms as seen from one side, filled and open for opposite sign and sized by weight; a bar is a p lobe in the page.\n\n**Not shown.** 6 core orbitals below −9.92 Hartree.
